**Weighting sensitivity (computed).** reserved_retrospective: largest |network-weighted - per-case| selection shift = 1.449 pp (calibrated_screen_70 @ 20.0 C; per-case +0.395 pp vs network-weighted +1.844 pp); wave2_designed: largest |network-weighted - per-case| selection shift = 0.234 pp (interval_abstention @ 20.0 C; per-case +1.740 pp vs network-weighted +1.506 pp). The per-case selection shift is invariant to the weighting only for `reconstruct_all` (where p_A = p_full under every weighting); for the other rules the magnitude can move by ~1 pp or more. Sign disagreements between per-case and network-weighted occur in 3 of 28 pooled rule x threshold x panel cells: reserved_retrospective @ 18.0 C elev_balanced_screen_70 (per-case -0.128 pp -> network-weighted +0.784 pp); reserved_retrospective @ 20.0 C elev_balanced_and_abstention (per-case -0.061 pp -> network-weighted +0.997 pp); reserved_retrospective @ 20.0 C elev_balanced_screen_70 (per-case -0.015 pp -> network-weighted +1.135 pp) (2 of these have |value| >= 0.05 pp on both weightings, so they are not rounding artefacts). The flipped cells are exactly the elevation-balanced rules on the reserved panel: step 8's headline quote of a small hot-share trade-off there (`hot_share_bias_pp ~ -0.13 pp` at 18.0 C) is a per-case artefact and must not be quoted as evidence of a cost-free elevation-balanced screen.

**Arm sensitivity (computed, per case, 18.0 C).** reserved_retrospective arm=empirical: selection shift spans +0.869 to +2.683 pp (largest for screen70_and_abstention); reserved_retrospective arm=stratified: selection shift spans -2.746 to +1.378 pp (largest for interval_abstention); wave2_designed arm=empirical: selection shift spans +0.033 to +0.272 pp (largest for screen70_and_abstention); wave2_designed arm=stratified: selection shift spans -0.014 to +1.069 pp (largest for screen70_and_abstention). The empirical arms are the realistic ones (real observed-overlap gaps), and their selection shifts are the ones a monitoring application would face; the designed stratified arms are larger and partly negative.

