### F03 verdict in plain terms

- **Which cells have a non-binding 0.5% budget?** 1 of 4 panel x threshold cells: wave2_designed @ 18.0 C (52/13017 = 0.3995%). In those cells every 'complete' rule family (screens at full retention, abstention at zero-width interval) reaches coverage 1.00 inside the budget, so the coverage-maximising equal-budget answer is judge-everything and screening/abstention cannot be called better; abstention can only reproduce it.
- **When the 0.5% budget binds** (judge-everything is outside it), the rule with the largest coverage inside the budget is:
  - reserved_retrospective @ 18.0 C: interval_abstention (coverage 96.12%, 52 wrong = 0.4806% of all candidates)
  - reserved_retrospective @ 20.0 C: interval_abstention (coverage 94.80%, 53 wrong = 0.4898% of all candidates)
  - wave2_designed @ 20.0 C: interval_abstention (coverage 96.74%, 64 wrong = 0.4917% of all candidates)
- **At equal coverage** (identical coverage for every family, by interpolation) the abstention rules have the lowest error in the cells reported below — which is the second half of F03's requirement: abstention can look better than a screen only when coverage is held fixed.

  - reserved_retrospective @ 18.0 C, coverage 0.70: interval_abstention (0 wrong in 7574 decided = 0.0000%)
  - reserved_retrospective @ 20.0 C, coverage 0.70: interval_abstention (0 wrong in 7574 decided = 0.0000%)
  - wave2_designed @ 18.0 C, coverage 0.70: interval_abstention (2 wrong in 9112 decided = 0.0219%)
  - wave2_designed @ 20.0 C, coverage 0.70: screen_and_abstention (2 wrong in 9112 decided = 0.0219%)

- **Why zero-width abstention does not always reach coverage 1.00:** a zero-width interval still abstains when the point estimate equals the threshold exactly, so the abstention family's maximum coverage is reserved_retrospective @ 18.0 C = 0.99972; reserved_retrospective @ 20.0 C = 1.00000; wave2_designed @ 18.0 C = 1.00000; wave2_designed @ 20.0 C = 1.00000. The shortfall is a handful of exact ties, and it is reported rather than rounded away.

